Make the GLX Mesa context backend's exported functions weak so the embed
library can supply its own backend (embed/mglcntx_embed.c, EGL pbuffer) in
the same link while qemu-system keeps GLX. The two are never both strong:
qemu-system links only this file, libqemu-embed links both.

diff -Nru a/hw/mesa/mglcntx_linux.c b/hw/mesa/mglcntx_linux.c
--- a/hw/mesa/mglcntx_linux.c	2026-09-02 22:31:35.925479984 -0300
+++ b/hw/mesa/mglcntx_linux.c	2026-09-02 22:31:35.941871462 -0300
@@ -30,11 +30,14 @@
     if (cond) { fprintf(stderr, "glcntx: " fmt "\n" , ## __VA_ARGS__); }
 
